WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.029
Director Zack Snyder's 4-hour long cut of
Justice League has finally seen the light

00:00:05.029 --> 00:00:06.750
of earth's yellow sun.

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:12.500
When Snyder had to step away from the DC Extended
Universe's all star team-up in 2016 after

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:18.460
a tragedy in his family, Warner Bros. enlisted
Avengers writer-director Joss Whedon to finish

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:19.460
the film.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.640
Whedon's version of Justice League was not
well received on release.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:26.300
It was panned critically and bombed at the
box office.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:31.650
The reputation of Whedon himself has also
soured among the eyes of many amid accusations

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:37.640
that his Justice League reshoot set was, in
the words of Cyborg actor Ray Fisher, "gross,

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:40.890
abusive, unprofessional, and completely unacceptable."

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:44.090
"Booyah."

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:49.090
Fans rallied for Warner Bros. to "Release
The Snyder Cut" — a once far-fetched wish

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:52.320
that's finally come true on HBO Max.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:56.750
Most of the main Justice League stars were
quick to come out in favor of the Snyder Cut,

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:01.170
including Jason Momoa , Ben Affleck, Gal Gadot
, and Ray Fisher.

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:07.270
But Henry Cavill , who first played Superman
in Snyder's 2013 film, Man of Steel, had mostly

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:11.890
stayed silent on the subject of the Snyder
Cut — until now.

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:18.159
In a March 18, 2021 Instagram post, Henry
Cavill congratulated Zack Snyder on the fulfilment

00:01:18.159 --> 00:01:21.069
of his vision for the DC Extended Universe.

00:01:21.069 --> 00:01:22.069
The star wrote,

00:01:22.069 --> 00:01:23.509
"Here's to you Zack.

00:01:23.509 --> 00:01:24.509
Congratulations!

00:01:24.509 --> 00:01:28.110
I know this has been an arduous journey for
you, you kept fighting, though.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:31.860
I couldn't be happier to see your vision for
Justice League realised.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.479
And what a movie it is!"

00:01:33.479 --> 00:01:39.049
Cavill knows a lot about fighting to see something
get made; he was originally cast in a Superman

00:01:39.049 --> 00:01:44.850
movie back in 2004 that was set to be directed
by the filmmaker McG , and even got as close

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:47.939
as having a fitting for Superman's iconic
cape.

00:01:47.939 --> 00:01:53.280
But when Bryan Singer took over the project
for what ultimately became Superman Returns,

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.770
he cast Brandon Routh in the role.

00:01:55.770 --> 00:02:01.009
Cavill also used the #HopeNeverDies hashtag,
in reference to his character's slogan in

00:02:01.009 --> 00:02:02.670
promotion for the film.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:08.509
Superman's logo, in some versions of comics
lore, isn't a big S; it's actually the Kryptonian

00:02:08.509 --> 00:02:10.280
symbol for hope.

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:14.790
Superman explains the symbol to Lois Lane
in Man of Steel, and further elaborates in

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:18.650
the Whedon cut of Justice League that it takes
its shape from a river.

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:26.702
“The symbol of the house of El means hope;
embodied in that hope is the fundamental belief

00:02:26.702 --> 00:02:28.700
in the potential of every person to be a force
for good."

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:33.480
When asked about the Snyder Cut previously,
Henry Cavill has played somewhat coy.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:38.080
When asked by entertainment reporter Jake
Hamilton why he had remained silent while

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:42.720
the rest of the cast joined the call for the
Snyder Cut, Cavill said he declined to speak

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.069
for a decidedly unserious reason.

00:02:45.069 --> 00:02:46.069
He said,

00:02:46.069 --> 00:02:49.360
"I miss my mustache — which is the most
important thing.

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:53.920
And for me, it was just a harrowing reminder
that I didn't have it anymore.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:57.069
And so I just didn't want to dig that wound
any deeper."

00:02:57.069 --> 00:03:01.620
Cavill grew the 'stache for Mission: Impossible
— Fallout and was legally prevented from

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:04.590
being allowed to shave it off during the Justice
League reshoots.

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:08.069
"Well, I knew you didn't bring me back because
you liked me."

00:03:08.069 --> 00:03:13.230
The result, as many know, was that producers
spent millions digitally removing the mustache

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:16.200
from every frame of Superman's screen time.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:21.190
The final effect flew Supes right into the
uncanny valley for many viewers, so you'd

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:26.409
think Cavill would at least be happy to finally
have his real face in the spotlight in Zack

00:03:26.409 --> 00:03:28.159
Snyder's Justice League.

00:03:28.159 --> 00:03:33.360
Producers at DC and Warner Bros. are currently
maintaining that the Snyder Cut is not canon

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:39.540
in the DCEU, so Clark Kent's fate hasn't really
changed between now and 2017.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:44.680
But the critical acclaim being thrown at Zack
Snyder's Justice League may change that.

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:49.350
As columnist Owen Gleiberman wrote in his
review of the film for Variety,

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:54.760
"Zack Snyder's Justice League is the movie
that shows us, at last, what the DCEU could

00:03:54.760 --> 00:04:00.380
be ... Now that that's happened, to leave
Snyder by the wayside seems not merely unjust;

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:02.489
it strikes me as foolhardy."

00:04:02.489 --> 00:04:07.079
In other words, some critics think that Warner
Bros. should think twice about ignoring the

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:10.230
fanbase to which they just capitulated.

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:13.359
Henry Cavill has expressed interest in returning
to the role.

00:04:13.359 --> 00:04:15.849
As he told Men's Health in 2019,

00:04:15.849 --> 00:04:17.769
"The cape is in the closet.

00:04:17.769 --> 00:04:19.079
It's still mine."

